        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: OAuth refresh failures report reauth instead of stale success",
        "body": "Closes #99120\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users with managed OpenAI OAuth profiles could see auth appear healthy after a refresh failure when an external Codex CLI credential still existed but was stale or invalidated. This made operator status false-green and could require repeated pairing-code relogs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe OAuth manager now fails closed on refresh errors instead of falling back to external CLI credentials after refresh failure. External CLI credentials remain available only for the existing unusable-profile bootstrap path, and doctor/refresh-failure hints include the affected safe profile id without mutating model defaults.\n\nThis touches CODEOWNERS auth files and likely needs secops review.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators get an explicit reauth-required error for the affected profile instead of a misleading successful auth state. Doctor output can point at the exact profile to relog without changing the user's default model.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-manager.test.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-refresh-failure.test.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth.openai-codex-refresh-fallback.test.ts src/commands/doctor-auth.hints.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-execution.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-refresh-failure.test.ts`\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/agents/auth-profiles/external-cli-sync.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-manager.test.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-manager.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-refresh-failure.test.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-refresh-failure.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth.openai-codex-refresh-fallback.test.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth.ts src/commands/doctor-auth.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --base origin/main --prompt <auth refresh fallback scope>`: clean, no accepted/actionable findings",
        "branch": "fix/oauth-managed-refresh-external-fallback-99120",
